# --- third-party material, never part of this deliverable ------------------
# The old single-model Flask demo + notebooks that 08_webapp/ was modeled on
# and improves upon. Kept out of the repo deliberately (see 08_webapp/README.md).
temp/

# --- large regenerable data artifacts --------------------------------------
# Too large to track usefully, and every one of them is rebuilt by re-running
# the pipeline. Every SMALL artifact (metrics, plots, best-params, the final
# report, the trained model .pkl files) stays committed, so the results remain
# browsable on GitHub without a clone + full re-run. See dataset/README.md and
# outputs/README.md for how to rebuild these.
#
#   dataset/usgs_earthquake_catalog.csv           (~46MB, grows every stage-01 fetch)
#   outputs/03_processed/03_cleaned_catalog.csv   (~51MB)
#   outputs/04_features/04_feature_matrix.csv     (~557MB; 7 horizon_day rows per
#                                                  (cell, day) since the multi-horizon
#                                                  target change)
#   outputs/02_profiling/usgs_earthquake_profile.json  (~107MB; the human-readable
#                                                  .html sibling IS committed)
dataset/usgs_earthquake_catalog.csv
outputs/03_processed/03_cleaned_catalog.csv
outputs/04_features/04_feature_matrix.csv
outputs/02_profiling/usgs_earthquake_profile.json

# Ad-hoc stdout capture from a manual stage-01 run, not a pipeline artifact.
outputs/01_fetch_log.txt

# Experiment feature matrices (magnitude-threshold sensitivity study, stage 09).
# Same ~557MB-per-matrix problem as the main one above; the small backtest
# RESULTS under outputs/experiments/*/09_backtest/ stay committed.
#   -> regenerate: python scripts/04_feature_engineering.py --mag-threshold 5.0 \
#        --output ../outputs/experiments/mag5.0/04_feature_matrix.csv ...
outputs/experiments/*/04_feature_matrix.csv

# --- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Maps API key for the stage-08 dashboard. The reference app this UI was
# taken from had a live key written directly into its page source; this repo is
# public, so the key is read at render time from this untracked file instead
# (see 08_webapp/app.py). Create it yourself with your own key as the only
# contents - one line, no quotes.
08_webapp/.google_maps_key
